## Critical Patterns

### IPC Communication
```typescript
// Main: Always return { success: boolean, ...data } or { success: false, error: string }
ipcMain.handle('example', async () => {
  try {
    return { success: true, data: result };
  } catch (error) {
    log.error('Error:', error);
    return { success: false, error: (error as Error).message };
  }
});

// Preload: Expose in types.d.ts AND index.ts
// types.d.ts
interface ElectronAPI {
  example: () => Promise<{ success: boolean; data?: any; error?: string }>;
}
// index.ts
example: () => ipcRenderer.invoke('example'),

// Renderer: Call via ElectronService, wrap async results in ngZone.run()
async doSomething() {
  const result = await this.electronService.example();
  this.ngZone.run(() => {
    this.data = result.data;
    this.cdr.detectChanges();  // Force UI update after async
  });
}
```

### Event Subscriptions (Main → Renderer)
```typescript
// ElectronService: Use shared Subjects, setup once in constructor
private example$ = new Subject<void>();
constructor() {
  this.electronAPI.onExample(() => this.example$.next());
}
onExample(): Observable<void> {
  return this.example$.asObservable();
}

// Component: Subscribe in setupEventListeners()
this.electronService.onExample().subscribe(() => {
  this.handleExample();
});
```

### Angular Change Detection
- **ALWAYS** wrap state updates after `await` in `this.ngZone.run(() => { ... })`
- **ALWAYS** call `this.cdr.detectChanges()` after updating component state from async operations
- This prevents the "double-click to work" bug

